## English

## 1. Overview

RailVideoTrim (hereinafter referred to as “the Software”) is software designed to automatically detect the desired segments from videos recorded during railway filming or similar activities by analyzing changes in the footage, and to extract those segments.

The Software is provided free of charge.

This License sets forth the terms and conditions for using the Software.

---

## 2. Permitted Use

Provided you comply with the terms of this license, the following uses are permitted free of charge:

- Use of the Software by individuals for their own personal purposes
- Use of the Software by corporations or organizations for business purposes
- Processing videos filmed or produced for commercial purposes using the Software
- Promoting the Software
- Posting a link to the Software’s official distribution page

You are free to use, publish, sell, or otherwise dispose of video files created using this software.

---

## 3. Redistribution

Redistributing the executable files, installers, or other distribution materials of this software to third parties is prohibited.

This includes the following actions:

- Distributing this software on your own website or blog
- Distributing this software using file-sharing services
- Uploading distribution files for this software to social media, message boards, forums, etc.
- Directly providing this software to third parties as a file
- Distributing media containing this software to third parties

As a general rule, please download this software from the official GitHub repository and official GitHub Releases.

If a third party wishes to introduce this software, please do not repost the distribution files; instead, provide a link to the official distribution page.

